# The blobs in this repository are LF, and the generated output committed under src/generated/ and
# dist/ was produced from an LF working tree. A clone made with core.autocrlf=true - git's default
# on Windows - checks the sources out as CRLF, the generators then embed `\r\n` inside JSON string
# values, and check-generated / check-runtime-index / check-schema fail on a fresh clone. Those are
# escape sequences inside strings, not line terminators, so git's own conversion cannot even them
# out. Pin the working tree to LF on every platform instead.
* text=auto eol=lf
